!! Text Editor

Template: `$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-editor`

Wraps `<$edit-text>` with EditorToolbar children so the framed editor engine binds keyboard shortcuts (bold, italic, headings, autolist if `sq/editor-autolist` is installed). Adds a hidden ''leave edit mode'' toolbar item bound to Ctrl+Enter that clears the caller's edit-state tiddler.

|!Variable (via `<$let>`) |!Description |
|`editTiddler` |Title of the tiddler whose `text` field is being edited |
|`editState` |State tiddler that gates edit mode (cleared on Ctrl+Enter) |
|`wrapClass` |CSS class for the outer wrapper div (consumer-supplied, controls width/height) |

```
<$let editTiddler=<<myNote>> editState="$:/state/my-edit" wrapClass="my-editor">
<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-editor"/>
</$let>
```

The toolbar is hidden via `.rr-text-editor-host > .tc-editor-toolbar { display: none }` (added in this plugin). Shortcuts still fire because TW core's `framed.js` engine looks them up via `querySelectorAll("[data-tw-keyboard-shortcut]")` regardless of CSS visibility. Style the visible iframe via your `<<wrapClass>> iframe.tc-edit-texteditor` selector — the inner textarea is inside the iframe and not directly stylable from outside.

!! Double-click-to-edit

Template: `$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-view-editable`

Companion to `rr-text-editor`. Wraps a block-mode transclude in an `<$eventcatcher>` whose `$dblclick` sets the caller's `editState` tiddler to `"yes"`. Use it where the host already has an edit/view toggle so users get a discoverable gesture in addition to any toggle button.

|!Variable (via `<$let>`) |!Description |
|`editState` |State tiddler the `$dblclick` action sets to `"yes"` |
|`viewTiddler` |(Optional) tiddler to render in block mode. If blank, uses the surrounding `<$tiddler>`/currentTiddler context |

```
<$let editState=<<noteEditState>> viewTiddler=<<activeNote>>>
<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-view-editable" $mode="block"/>
</$let>
```

Renders as `<div class="rr-text-view-editable tc-eventcatcher">…</div>`. The class adds a subtle `cursor: text` hint; restyle by overriding the rule in your plugin.

